# Since B8 (plans/handover/VBD_LOOKAHEAD_2026-10-23.md §4.5) an `ArrayList` is a
# value: `self.items = fresh` moves the list, so the later `fresh.push` is a
# static E0901 instead of the runtime panic described below.
# Since decision 39 (plans/VALUES_BY_DEFAULT.md) the loop body cannot name the
# iterated collection (E0911), so the call goes through a second handle, which
# the static rule cannot see and the runtime borrow flag guards.
# plans/archive/INOUT_LOCAL_BINDINGS_AUDIT.md §9 third pass: the per-parameter mutation
# mask treats storage a method allocates itself as FRESH (mutating it is not a
# mutation of the collection) — but the moment that storage is stored into
# `self`, it is reachable from the parameter and every later mutation of it
# counts. `rebuild` builds a fresh list, stores it into `self.items`, then
# pushes into it: the method must carry the entry assert and panic under a
# live borrow. `build run` propagates the panic as rc≠0.
stdout_keep_match=error\[E0901\]: use of moved value: (cannot copy )?[^ ]+
timeout=300
